 ('Reading · A biography',bio('Katherine Johnson',['**Born** in West Virginia in 1918, Katherine Johnson showed a gift for numbers early. **Having graduated** from college at eighteen, she taught school. **Hired** by NASA’s predecessor in 1953, she **worked** on flight calculations. **Asked** to check a computer’s figures before a 1962 orbital flight, she confirmed them by hand.','**Receiving** the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2015, she **said** she had simply loved her work. She died in 2020.'],years='1918–2020',facts=[('Job','matemática'),('Country','Estados Unidos'),('Famous for','cálculos de trajetória da NASA')],gloss=[('gift','talento'),('flight','voo'),('figure','número'),('confirm','confirmar')])),
 [('Johnson was born in West Virginia.','T','West Virginia.'),('She graduated from college at thirty.','F','eighteen.'),('She received the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2015.','T','2015.')],
